WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.919
Sometimes your problem is that you have

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.080
this voice in your head that you think

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:07.919
is you and you think is rational and

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.679
reasonable, but it is lying to you every

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:10.719
single day. The scariest part is you

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:12.400
don't even know that it's happening

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.000
because you think the lies are your own

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.000
thoughts. I am about to walk you through

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.160
14 specific patterns your brain runs on

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.920
autopilot that are quietly keeping you

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.640
away from the life that you say you

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.720
want. Most people do not conquer the

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.960
voice in your head. And that is also why

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.880
nobody warns you about this except me

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.800
because at least I know the voice in my

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.559
head is a liar. Do I conquer it

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.000
sometimes? But at least I'm aware of

00:00:32.559 --> 00:00:36.000
these mind traps. And once you know

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.680
something, you can't unknow it. So this

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.200
video may actually change everything for

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.559
you. If you're into self-development,

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.239
psychology, and becoming the most

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:44.160
powerful version of yourself inside out,

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:45.760
welcome to my channel. My name is May.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.280
My podcast and community are called

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.800
Stoic Angels, and I talk about things

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.480
that actually change your life. I don't

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.000
like to sugarcoat things. I will give it

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.520
to you straight. If you want to go even

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.440
deeper and answer some additional

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.120
prompts I've made for you specifically

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.280
for each and every one of these mind

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.280
traps, you can download my free PDF

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.280
guide and workbook from the link in the

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.439
description. This is my gift to you. It

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.439
is a companion guide for this video, a

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:09.200
free resource, so go ahead and download

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:10.960
that if you haven't already. I also have

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.640
two degrees, one in design and the other

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.320
in psychology. the fact that I was

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.400
trying to maximize my chances of getting

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.159
a good job by getting multiple degrees

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.240
and ultimately still felt like for the

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:22.320
longest time I didn't put these degrees

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.640
to good use until I started this YouTube

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.479
channel only proves that the only thing

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.560
that we'll never lose is our knowledge

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:30.320
here's a quick reminder to stay in

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.560
school and get a degree if you can maybe

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.159
get two or three nothing is wasted on

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.680
gaining new knowledge and it is a

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:37.119
privilege that I got to learn what I

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.040
learned and I'm sharing this with you

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:40.880
today and I get to break it down for you

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.560
everyone deserves to know how our minds

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.560
work so that we can make them work for

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.840
us. Important disclaimer, my content is

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.280
never a diagnosis. It is not

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.560
psychotherapy. It is not clinical

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.640
advice. This is for educational

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.079
andformational purposes always. And

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.840
usually it's me sharing what I've

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:55.280
learned and what has helped me. Mind

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.280
trap number one, all or nothing

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.119
thinking. This one got me the most of

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.799
worst, down, bad, whatever. All or

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:02.719
nothing thinking is when you look at

00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:04.479
everything in extremes, black or white,

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:06.240
perfect or worthless, good or bad. It is

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:08.080
also known as the pendulum swing.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.520
Swinging from one extreme to the other.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.120
This means if you try to do something

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.360
and it wasn't flawless, you will see

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.120
yourself as an absolute failure. If you

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.400
give a presentation and it goes really

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.319
well and people are clapping for you,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.239
but you stumble on one sentence,

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:21.680
suddenly the whole thing was a mess. If

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.360
you're studying for an exam and you

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.040
don't get a perfect score, clearly you

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.480
are stupid. You'll say things like, "I

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.080
am ugly because my friend is prettier

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.080
than me." Or, "I can't do anything

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.080
right. Why am I so dumb?" If you hear

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.080
yourself like this, do you hear how

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.319
violent this language is? It is

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.319
extremely punishing. And that punishment

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:40.160
feels justified to you because those

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:43.280
impossible standards that you set for

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.319
yourself somehow also feel real to you,

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:48.400
but it is not real. This is a trap. Life

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:50.080
is never black and white or binary. You

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.080
are not the most amazing person in the

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.400
world, nor are you a piece of garbage.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.000
You are a human being on this floating

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.000
rock with a few billion other human

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.680
beings. And we're all constant works in

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.319
progress. Nobody's better or worse than

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.560
anyone else. And this progress is messy

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:06.400
by nature. times things get really tough

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.480
and we'll never feel prepared enough.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.200
But Salvie, not attempting something new

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:13.360
at all is even harder in hindsight. I

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.800
have lived in this trap for years and

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.040
there were things in my life that I

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.440
didn't want to change or try to because

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.959
I thought if I couldn't guarantee that I

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.879
would do it right, I shouldn't try at

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:24.480
all. I wouldn't seek out new ways to

00:03:22.879 --> 00:03:26.480
better my mental health, for example,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.080
because I thought it wasn't for me. I

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.159
would talk myself out of it. This

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.239
happened with many things that I regret

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:34.319
now not trying before. And it kept me

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:35.840
stuck because ultimately everything that

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:38.239
we do including the things that we don't

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.239
do has risk nothing is guaranteed except

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:42.080
for guaranteed failure. If we fail

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:44.799
ourselves before we even start because

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.879
that somehow feels safer. What helped me

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:49.680
start to break that pattern was going

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:51.760
through talk therapy. Having someone who

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.840
could reflect back to me the things I

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.159
couldn't see about my own thinking and

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.239
frame it in a way that is helpful.

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:00.480
Because the thing about mind traps is

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:03.040
you can't always catch them yourself.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.360
Sometimes our emotions get so tangled up

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.360
in the situation that you do need

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.599
someone outside of your head to say,

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.120
"Hey, have you ever considered that

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:13.360
that's not actually a fact, but a

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.120
pattern?" I realized I had a tendency to

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.280
run off to travel whenever there's a

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.000
problem, which isn't bad on its own, but

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.440
it is a form of escapism. BetterHelp is

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.520
the sponsor of today's video, and they

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.800
make starting therapy easier. All you

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.320
have to do is to take a quiz, get

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.080
matched with a licensed therapist, and

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.680
you can communicate however feels right

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.199
for you, whether that's through phone,

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.639
video, or text. If you'd like to try

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:34.880
another therapist, and find a better

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:36.880
fit, you can also switch anytime at no

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.560
extra cost. Over 6 million people have

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.800
gotten help through BetterHelp, and they

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.560
have a 4.8 out of five rating on the app

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.600
store. Click the link in the description

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.160
or go to my link at

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:48.479
betterhelp.com/mayalisuki

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.400
to get 10% off your first month. Mind

00:04:48.479 --> 00:04:52.560
trap number two, mental filtering.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.560
Mental filtering is when you take one

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.440
negative detail from a situation and you

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.919
fixate on that negativity so hard that

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.840
it overtakes everything else. This trap

00:04:59.919 --> 00:05:03.680
massively distorts your perception

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.000
before you even get a chance to think

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:08.160
clearly about any kind of situation.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.600
This is also why everyone sees different

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.680
realities. Even though you think that

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.840
yours may be the most objective one,

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.240
that is not always true and it is a hard

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:18.400
pill to swallow. This is going to sneak

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:20.240
up on you because it feels like you're

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.000
being logical. For example, you're

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:23.919
taking a class and you do a live demo or

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.680
a presentation. About 18 people tell

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:27.680
you, "Wow, that was great." And they're

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.400
giving you positive feedback. Then one

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.880
person makes a critical comment. Which

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.120
one lives in your head more? I think you

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.000
already know the answer to that. This is

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.680
a natural survival mechanism. Your brain

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.199
literally filters out all of the

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.039
evidence that things went well for you

00:05:41.199 --> 00:05:45.280
and magnifies a single one piece of

00:05:43.039 --> 00:05:47.199
evidence that confirms your worst

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.039
nightmare. That is like wearing rose

00:05:47.199 --> 00:05:51.520
tinted sunglasses, but instead of rose

00:05:49.039 --> 00:05:53.600
tinted, it's like hell tinted. You look

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:56.160
around and you say, "See, everything is

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.680
on fire. I'm in hell right now." No,

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.680
that's just what your filter looks like.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.280
The room itself actually has plenty of

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.840
good natural sunlight and you're just

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:06.160
blocking it with your hellfire mindset.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:07.600
Mind trap number three, magnification.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.360
This is what happens when you take

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.759
something really small and blow it up

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:13.520
into catastrophic proportions. Sometimes

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:15.600
you may notice this is also done in

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.520
tandem between you and another person

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:19.360
and you're both making things worse and

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.280
egging each other on. It's like a race

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.639
to the bottom. For example, you make a

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.639
mistake and immediately your brain

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:26.240
thinks I have ruined my reputation or

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:27.919
you accidentally send a text that wasn't

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.360
meant for the other person and suddenly

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.639
you think, "Oh my god, just destroy our

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.400
friendship." Your brain would take the

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:34.080
smallest issue like a pebble and bring

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.000
it back to you like as a massive

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.440
boulder. You respond to the boulder by

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.120
thinking that things are 100 times worse

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:41.440
than you're supposed to be. And so you

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.680
start panicking and you overcompensate.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.000
It starts to spiral over something that

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.400
is this tiny. So how do we catch

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.160
ourselves from spiraling even further? I

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:52.560
would just ask is this going to matter

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.400
to me in 5 years? If the answer is no,

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.080
then your brain is magnifying it.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.919
Recognize it, process it, and let it

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.800
pass. Mind trap number four,

00:06:57.919 --> 00:07:03.680
minimization. This is magnification's

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.919
evil twin. And in some ways, it's worse

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:08.639
because it really robs you of your happy

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:10.639
moments. Minimization is when you take

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:13.120
something that is really amazing or

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:15.120
genuinely good and you shrink it down to

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.880
nothing. For example, someone

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.720
congratulates you and you think, "Oh,

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.240
they just feel sorry for me." Or someone

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.319
calls you pretty and you think they're

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.919
just being nice. You manifest something

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:26.319
major or you hit a goal that you've been

00:07:23.919 --> 00:07:28.319
working on really hard and you think to

00:07:26.319 --> 00:07:30.720
yourself, "Well, it feels like nothing.

00:07:28.319 --> 00:07:32.800
It's like anyone can do this." This mind

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.800
trap shows up constantly, especially

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.720
with high achievers and people who grow

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.960
up being told that they were never good

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.120
enough. If that is you, pay extra

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.880
attention to this specific mind trap

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.880
because you are dismissing your own

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:47.120
evidence of your capabilities and your

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.759
potential. If you can't even acknowledge

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:52.000
your own progress, your brain will also

00:07:49.759 --> 00:07:54.720
not acknowledge it and people around you

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:56.080
will only follow your lead. Even if

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.400
you're moving forward and you're

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.800
achieving all of these amazing things,

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.960
you're refusing to let it count. And

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:06.400
this is going to steal your momentum. It

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:09.280
is so sneaky. We have to celebrate every

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:11.199
win and be grateful for our ability to

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.039
even accomplish something, even if it's

00:08:11.199 --> 00:08:14.800
tiny. This is why I have a gratitude

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:16.800
practice. Just naming a few things that

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.639
make me happy today, that I'm grateful

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.440
for, or that I'm happy I'm able to

00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:23.759
accomplish. This allows more moments in

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:25.759
your day for your brain to focus on your

00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:27.599
wins. Mind trap number five,

00:08:25.759 --> 00:08:30.160
overgeneralization.

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:31.680
You take one isolated negative incident

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:33.760
in your life and turn it into a

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.839
universal rule that applies to not just

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.279
you, but to everyone around you. If

00:08:35.839 --> 00:08:38.719
someone turns down your invitation to

00:08:37.279 --> 00:08:40.000
hang out, your brain doesn't think,

00:08:38.719 --> 00:08:41.279
well, maybe they have something going on

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.440
in your life you don't know about.

00:08:41.279 --> 00:08:45.600
Instead, you think, nobody wants to be

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:47.519
around me. I'm a loser. Or you go on one

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.000
bad date and you think, nobody wants me.

00:08:47.519 --> 00:08:51.680
So, I recently had a horrible bacterial

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.360
infection from a surgery where I almost

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:55.120
lost my life. I was talking about it

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.600
recently on another YouTube video and I

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:00.160
got so many comments saying things like,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.560
"Why did you go back to try and fix it?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.560
You are insane. You're so crazy." And

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.959
it's because I don't have this mind

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.519
trap, but the people who do will project

00:09:06.959 --> 00:09:11.760
it onto everyone else. Once bitten,

00:09:09.519 --> 00:09:13.680
twice shy. The same goes for people who

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.760
come across one of my more spiritual

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.279
woowoo videos and then they hear me

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:19.120
talking about glow and they're like, "I

00:09:17.279 --> 00:09:20.880
don't understand why you care about your

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:23.120
looks when you're so holy and

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:24.720
spiritual." I never said that. Remember

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:27.120
on my channel we talk about the

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.680
physical, mental, and spiritual and

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.080
everything is interconnected. So if you

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:34.000
hear language like always, never,

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:37.200
nobody, every single time, these

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.959
absolute words are huge, huge red flags.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.360
When you catch yourself using this type

00:09:38.959 --> 00:09:43.760
of language, you are overgeneralizing

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.519
and catastrophizing. One isolated

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:47.360
incident that happened to you or to

00:09:45.519 --> 00:09:49.200
someone that you know does not detect a

